---
import DocsLayout from '../../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Mono Workflow — MHA Manager"
  description="Process single-camera footage end to end: framing probe, optional body tracking, solve, and export."
  currentSlug="mono-workflow"
>

  <div class="doc-header">
    <span class="type-badge type-mono">Mono</span>
    <h1 class="doc-title">Mono Workflow</h1>
    <p class="doc-lead">
      Mono processes a single color camera — head-mounted or any single lens. It is the fastest job
      type and the right default: no calibration, identity, or depth. The realtime solver runs on the
      footage directly, with optional body tracking on UE 5.8.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="sub-heading">Required input</h2>
    <div class="asset-table">
      <div class="asset-row header"><span>Asset</span><span>Type</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>Capture Data</strong></span>
        <span><code>UFootageCaptureData</code></span>
        <span>Your video footage import — the only required input</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      No MetaHuman Identity or Camera Calibration needed. Get the Capture Data from
      <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/ingest">Ingest</a>, then add it to the queue.
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub-heading">Pipeline stages</h2>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Validate Input</span></div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Process Performance</span><span class="stage-note">Tracking + Fitting</span></div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Export Outputs</span></div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Save Assets</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="type-desc" style="margin-top: 12px;">
      With body tracking enabled, the body solve (detect -&gt; 2D keypoints -&gt; 3D pose -&gt; merge)
      runs after the face solve, before export.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Take auto-categorization — the framing probe (UE 5.8+)</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      When a Mono job is queued, MHA Manager probes the take's first frame with a pose model and
      classifies its framing, applying the right solve template automatically:
    </p>
    <div class="option-list">
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Full body</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Hips and ankles confidently visible — Body Tracking is enabled on the freshly queued job.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Upper body / Headshot</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Ankles cut off, or face only — the job stays face-only, with an amber warning if you enable body tracking anyway. The 5.8 body solver invents joints below the frame edge on a headshot, so this guard matters.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Not analyzed</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Nothing confidently visible, or the probe is unavailable — the job stays face-only with no badge.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="type-desc" style="margin: 16px 0 12px;">
      The verdict is advisory — it never overrides your choice or flips a running job.
      <strong>Re-check</strong> re-runs the probe; the verdict persists in the manifest so re-loaded
      queues do not re-probe. If frame 1 shows nothing (slates, subject stepping in), a fallback probe
      runs at ~25% into the take.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-note">
      <strong>Requirements:</strong> UE 5.8+, the <strong>MetaHumanBodyTracker</strong> plugin, and
      the <strong>NNERuntimeORT</strong> plugin enabled. When any is missing the probe quietly reports
      "Not analyzed". After any body-tracked solve the job also reports <strong>body coverage</strong>
      — below 80% it gets a "Body track gaps" warning, since undetected frames export as held pose.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="sub-heading">Face options</h2>
    <div class="option-list">
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Head Stabilization</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Corrects for head-movement drift during the solve. Enabled by default; disable only if it degrades a locked-off, tripod-style take.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Tongue Solve</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Enables tongue tracking. Requires UE 5.7+ and close framing with good lighting. Disabled by default.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Neutral Pose Calibration</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Uses a neutral expression frame to calibrate the facial geometry baseline before solving, with a blend weight (alpha).</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Body Tracking (UE 5.8+)</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      Mono jobs can optionally solve body motion alongside the face, using the SMPLX-based body
      tracker. Requires the <strong>MetaHumanBodyTracker</strong> plugin. Choose Face only, Body only,
      or Face + Body per job.
    </p>
    <div class="option-list">
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Body / Face Tracking</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Toggle each solve independently. Disable Face Tracking for a body-only run to save solve time.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Body Height</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Auto-infers subject height from footage by default (Epic recommends 145-190cm); disable Auto Body Height to pin a fixed value.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Detection / Tracking Confidence</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Thresholds for acquiring a body lock (default 0.7) and maintaining it (default 0.5). Lower detection for dim/cluttered footage; lower tracking if lock drops during fast motion.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Foot Locking, Head Rotation Limits</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Stabilizes foot contact, and sets yaw/pitch limits (defaults 45deg / 30deg) beyond which a frame falls back to a neutral head pose or is left unsolved.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Body export</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      A body-tracked solve exports onto either its own performer-shaped mesh or an existing skeleton.
    </p>
    <div class="option-list">
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Body Export Skeleton</span>
        <span class="option-desc"><strong>Performer Skeleton</strong> builds a mesh matching the solve's own body-shape betas. <strong>Existing Skeleton</strong> retargets the solved body onto a mesh you choose, via an IK Retargeter.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Target Mesh + Retargeter</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Shown for Existing Skeleton. Use <strong>+ Create Retargeter...</strong> to auto-generate one pre-wired to the SMPL body-tracker source rig — you only configure the target chain mapping.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Visualization Blueprint</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Body-tracked jobs need an Actor Blueprint (not a plain mesh) for the A|B viewport, since one mesh can't carry both Face and Body. Use <strong>Create Blueprint...</strong> to auto-build one that leader-poses Face to Body.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Unsolved Frames</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Fallback for frames the tracker couldn't solve: hold the last valid frame, or fall back to a neutral pose.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      See <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/job-options#body-tracking">Per-Job Options</a> for the
      full Body Tracking, Body Export, and Visualization reference.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="sub-heading">Outputs</h2>
    <div class="asset-table">
      <div class="asset-row header"><span>Output</span><span>When</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>Performance + AnimSequence</strong></span>
        <span>Always</span>
        <span>Solved performance plus baked face animation on the MetaHuman skeleton</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>Body animation</strong></span>
        <span>Body tracking on</span>
        <span>Exported per skeleton mode — performer skeleton, retargeted existing skeleton, or both passes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>FBX exports</strong></span>
        <span>Optional</span>
        <span>Enabled in Global Settings; body-tracking jobs get the baked-joint <code>_DCC</code> form</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="doc-footer">
    <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/ingest" class="prev-link">
      <span class="nav-label">Previous</span>
      <span class="nav-title">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5M12 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
        Ingest Footage
      </span>
    </a>
    <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/stereo-workflow" class="next-link">
      <span class="nav-label">Next</span>
      <span class="nav-title">
        Stereo Workflow
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .doc-figure { margin: 20px 0 4px; }
  .doc-img-placeholder {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 80%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 36px 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .placeholder-icon { color: var(--text-muted); opacity: 0.35; }
  .placeholder-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.775rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .placeholder-hint { font-size: 0.775rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 480px; line-height: 1.5; }
  figcaption { font-size: 0.775rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-align: center; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }

  .doc-header { margin-bottom: 40px; }

  .type-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .type-mono  { background: color-mix(in srgb, #4a9eff 12%, transparent); color: #4a9eff; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #4a9eff 30%, transparent); }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .doc-lead {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 620px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .doc-lead code, .type-desc code, .callout code, .asset-row code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .type-section {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .type-section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

  .type-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .sub-heading {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 24px 0 10px;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .asset-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .asset-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1.3fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .asset-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .asset-row.header {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .asset-row strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .pipeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin: 4px 0 8px;
  }

  .pipeline-stage {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .stage-name { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }
  .stage-note { font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .pipeline-arrow { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); }

  .option-list {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .option-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 2fr;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .option-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .option-name { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.825rem; }
  .option-desc { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  .option-desc strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .callout {
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 16px 0;
    border-left: 3px solid;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .callout-tip  { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .callout-note { background: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 8%, transparent); border-color: #f0a500; }
  .callout strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .callout code { color: var(--accent); }

  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .doc-footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .prev-link, .next-link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
    min-width: 140px;
  }

  .prev-link { align-items: flex-start; }
  .next-link { align-items: flex-end; }
  .prev-link:hover, .next-link:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

  .nav-label { font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--text-muted); }

  .nav-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .asset-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .asset-row span:last-child { display: none; }
    .asset-row.header span:last-child { display: none; }
    .option-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
